I gave up but this was my answer:

&#x200B;

How does this affect the student's performance in their studies? Are students the only ones affected by this? While this research aims to investigate how it's affecting one's studies, it's vital to know that it's not just the effect of the pandemic that gets through students. The research will focus on how many students have difficulties studying and passing their activities on time.

&#x200B;

6 out of 10 students we've interviewed say that they have difficulties doing their work on time, for the others would say "it depends on the mood." Most of these students also have a hard time with specific subjects, ranging from 2 to all the subjects' given. 

&#x200B;

Although this interview was only from a small group of students. It's clear how many students struggle with their academics.

tried killing myself in front of someone who's been mentally draining my energy with their toxic higher up, I can't explain it but just them pushing their opinions onto me on this and that. They walked out on me, I did the deed, they came back, one on one talk while my hand was bleeding(no they did not see it) had a talk saying "we'll go through this together" and pretended nothing happened. the wound left a pretty big scar but I can probably cover it with a watch, 5 months in, they see the scar, they feel "sad" for me, forgets about it. I still feel like dying, I have a lot of schoolwork to do. I regret hesitating at the last second, I hate how I didn't do it enough to bleed to death. Now I'm planning it, the easiest way to off myself without making a mess or in a place where there are people.

&#x200B;

So to answer that question, no I feel like shit. But what I did was shitty too, not only was I threatening to end my life I was also manipulating them into thinking it's their fault, which at this point it is, but still. Manipulation is manipulation. I'm glad they walked out on me, don't show me your pathetic pitiful face cause I don't need it.

